==German==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|de|be|stellen}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/bəˈʃtɛlən/|[bəˈʃtɛlən]|[-ˈʃtɛl̩n]}}
* {{audio|de|De-bestellen.ogg|audio}}
* {{hyphenation|de|be|stel|len}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|usually|transitive}} to [[order]] (e.g. food at a restaurant, items for delivery)
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''bestelle''' Bier für alle.|I'm '''ordering''' beer for everyone.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[order]] to come, to [[summon]]
#: {{syn|de|herbeirufen|herbeizitieren|beordern}}
# {{lb|de|usually|transitive}} to [[reserve]] (e.g. a table, hotel room)
#: {{syn|de|reservieren}}
# {{lb|de|ditransitive}} to [[convey]] to, to [[send]] to (a message, greetings)
#: {{syn|de|ausrichten}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[appoint]]
#: {{syn|de|berufen|bestimmen|ernennen}}
#: {{ux|de|Sie wurde zur neuen Pressesprecherin '''bestellt'''.|She was '''appointed''' as the new press secretary.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|agriculture}} to [[cultivate]], [[till]] (a field, by [[plough]]ing, [[manure|manuring]] etc.)
#: {{ux|de|Ein guter Bauer '''bestellt''' den Boden, bevor er pflanzt.|A good farmer '''cultivates''' the soil before planting.}}

